1590969600,-12.28],[1593561600,-5.56],[1596240000,-0.51],[1598918400,11.28],[1601510400,21.29],[1604188800,7.17],[1606780800,18.46],[1609459200,13.02],[1612137600,14.89],[1614556800,81.58],[1617235200,366.33],[1619827200,61.64],[1622505600,39.05],[1625097600,42.22],[1627776000,42.12],[1630454400,28.52],[1635724800,23.0],[1638316800,32.93],[1640995200,21.93],[1643673600,22.78],[1646092800,23.25],[1648771200,36.95],[1651363200,67.02],[1654041600,34.18],[1656633600,18.58],[1659312000,18.04],[1661990400,20.05],[1667260800,24.0],[1669852800,4.46],[1672531200,13.99],[1675209600,11.27],[1677628800,8.86],[1680307200,2.55],[1682899200,9.47],[1685577600,7.01],[1688169600,8.58],[1690848000,11.79],[1693526400,7.6],[1696118400,20.81],[1698796800,1.8],[1701388800,7.04],[1704067200,9.29],[1706745600,12.4],[1709251200,7.43],[1711929600,6.94],[1714521600,11.61],[1717200000,10.22],[1719792000,11.7],[1722470400,6.19],[1725148800,10.81],[1727740800,10.56],[1730419200,12.25],[1733011200,11.04],[1735689600,16.89],[1738368000,7.73],[1740787200,14.61],[1743465600,15.87],[1746057600,11.02],[1748736000,11.15],[1751328000,15.72],[1754006400,13.42],[1756684800,16.02],[1759276800,4.72],[1761955200,20.56],[1764547200,25.93],[1767225600,14.69],[1769904000,20.44],[1772323200,16.96],[1775001600,18.98],[1777593600,20.31],[1780272000,33.46],[1782864000,25.23],[1785542400,27.74]]}]}],"qna":[{"question":"What is this series?","answer":"The number of e-way bills generated in a month, summed over all States and UTs, and the assessable (taxable) value of the goods covered. Total = within-state bills + bills for goods going out to other states. 'Incoming from other states' is the same inter-state bills seen from the receiving state, so it is not added.^Counts are plain numbers (a recent month is above 100 million) and values are in Rs. crore. Monthly statistics start July 2018 (e-way bills became compulsory for inter-state movement in April 2018)."},{"question":"How should I read it?","answer":"Year-on-year growth in bill counts tracks the physical movement of goods; value growth also reflects prices and the mix of goods. Seasonality is marked: March (year-end) is high and festival and monsoon months move the series, so compare the same month across years.^It is a coincident indicator for goods trade, manufacturing dispatches and wholesale activity and tends to move with GST collections and industrial output."},{"question":"Caveats and revisions?","answer":"Thresholds, state rules for intra-state bills (phased in during 2018) and the mix of goods covered have changed over time, so growth in 2018-19 is partly a roll-out effect.^One consignment can generate more than one bill, so counts are not distinct shipments. October 2021 is omitted because the published file shows near-zero within-state bills for Maharashtra, Gujarat and Tamil Nadu that month (a reporting defect). Data are as published by GSTN and may be revised. The statistics files are monthly only; no daily series is published there."}],"related":[],"layer":"added","note":"Monthly state-wise file summed over States/UTs; total = within-state + outgoing inter-state bills. These totals run about 0.5-1.4% below the headline figures GSTN announces for the same months, so the two compilations differ slightly. October 2021 is omitted because the source file is defective for that month.","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T07:24:40+00:00"}